# pc-surf-key (BENCH-160): c is master, aa its A/A copy; kl plays the fitted surf keys (SKEY-2: nine key-weight multipliers
# and the kernel width) against the robots the fit shipped a key for, klbb the weights-only keys (width 1). bb only names
# the second build apart; it changes nothing.
c | hadur117.Hadur 3.20 | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.20.jar
aa | hadur117.Hadur 3.20aa | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.20aa.jar
kl | hadur117.Hadur 3.20kl | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.20kl.jar
klbb | hadur117.Hadur 3.20klbb | bisect/hadur117.Hadur_3.20klbb.jar
